            <ArticleTitle>Hemorrhagic ovarian cyst in childhood: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>978-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 12-year-old girl with massive hemoperitoneum caused by a ruptured hemorrhagic ovarian cyst (HOC) is described. Although HOC is not common in early adolescence, it should be included in the differential diagnosis of any adnexal mass or lower abdominal pain in a girl.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
